{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bacteroid-computable-vole","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py:319-357` and `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:529-559` duplicate fallback, direction, deduplication, and observation construction. `jira_family/link_direction.py:1-58` records prior one-sided drift.\n\n## Approach\n\nPlace one pure canonicalizer beside the existing Jira-family direction seam. It parses raw `issuelinks`, determines inward/outward direction, handles malformed or unmapped links, deduplicates, and returns canonical link observations. Cloud and Data Center keep separate transports and delegate to it. The provider-neutral desired-versus-observed diff remains unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Jira Cloud and Data Center adapter link extraction\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/jira_family/link_direction.py`\n- shared behavior vectors and adapter delegation tests\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch consumers before moving behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun identical vectors through both adapters for inward/outward links, malformed payloads, unmapped types, duplicates, and empty input.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] One pure Jira-family function owns link parsing, direction, fallback, deduplication, and canonical observation construction.\n- [ ] Cloud and Data Center transports remain separate and both delegate to the shared function.\n- [ ] Shared vectors prove both delegates produce identical canonical observations for all supported and fallback cases.\n- [ ] Provider-neutral relation contracts and desired-versus-observed diff behavior remain unchanged.","id":"a07a-5eeb-1223-491c","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","jira","architecture","rp10"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Centralize Jira-family link canonicalization across Cloud and Data Center"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311582971759001,"uuid":"649856d0-799b-4ac5-b622-0b17d55b379d"}